        "original_id": "a8a375d3-f046-59ab-bcb6-775a5f03ccc0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark E. Mitchell\n- Events: Battle of Qala-i-Jangi\n- Places: northern Afghanistan\n- Organizations: United States-led coalition forces, Taliban, al-Qaeda\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Qala-i-Jangi was a prisoner-of-war camp uprising that took place in northern Afghanistan between November 25 and December 1, 2001.\n- The Battle of Qala-i-Jangi is sometimes incorrectly referred to as the Battle of Mazar-i-Sharif.\n- United States-led coalition forces intervened in Afghanistan to try to overthrow the Taliban's Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan, which they accused of harboring al-Qaeda operatives.\n- In 2003, Mark E. Mitchell received an award for his actions during the Battle of Qala-i-Jangi.",
